  "notes": "Mask-constrained Kontext replacement with IP-Adapter identity conditioning (v0.3.1). The BASE image (current room state) feeds VAEEncodeForInpaint whose noise mask confines sampling to the affected region - unmasked pixels keep the base exactly. The REFERENCE stays conditioning-only: node 12 ReferenceLatent takes its latent from node 20 (VAEEncodeForInpaint of the base scene) instead of node 8 (VAEEncode of the stretched reference crop), so the locality hint comes from the base frame rather than injecting a whole-frame reference wash (nodes 8/16 remain in the graph but are no longer consumed); identity transfer is carried solely by the Shakker-Labs comfyui-ipadapter-flux nodes: node 25 loads the CROPPED reference (control_image role, same asset as reference_image), node 24 IPAdapterFluxLoader loads ip-adapter.bin plus the google/siglip-so400m-patch14-384 CLIP-Vision encoder (provider cuda) and outputs IP_ADAPTER_FLUX_INSTANTX, and node 27 ApplyIPAdapterFlux patches the UNET (model from node 3) with that adapter and the cropped reference image before KSampler 13; node 27's weight input is driven by ipa_weight at execution time. The mask PNG (white=edit region, linear feather ramp baked in server-side) binds through ImageToMask(red). Node inputs verified against the box fork object_info (v9.1): ImageToMask(image,channel), VAEEncodeForInpaint(pixels,vae,mask,grow_mask_by 0..64), ConditioningSetMask(conditioning,mask,strength,set_cond_area); FeatherMask node deliberately not used (no single feather input - feathering is baked into the mask PNG server-side)."
